WIZ RUNTIME LIBRARY EXCEPTION

Version 1.0, 11 November 2026

This Wiz Runtime Library Exception ("Exception") is an additional permission
under section 7 of the GNU General Public License, version 3 ("GPLv3"). It
applies to the Runtime Library, defined below, which is part of Wiz and is
licensed under the GNU General Public License, either version 3 of the
License, or (at your option) any later version ("the GPL"). The text of the
GPL is in the file LICENSE.

When you convey a copy of the Runtime Library, or a work based on it, you may
at your option remove this Exception from that copy, as section 7 of GPLv3
permits.

0. Definitions.

"Wiz" means the software in this repository: the Wiz compilers, checkers and
kernels (including the self-hosted ones), the build tool grail, the toolchain
manager tower, the editor support, the libraries and the runtime.

The "Runtime Library" means those parts of Wiz that end up inside, or are
combined with, the programs that Wiz compiles:

  (a) the files under runtime/;
  (b) the file selfhost/rt.c;
  (c) the files under lib/;
  (d) the prelude that the self-hosted front end carries inside it (the
      definitions that every program compiled by it starts from); and
  (e) any other portion of Wiz that a Wiz compiler copies into its output, or
      emits as part of its output, when it compiles a program, such as
      runtime support code, code templates and foreign-function glue.

The Runtime Library does not include the rest of Wiz. In particular it does
not include the compilers, checkers and kernels themselves, grail, tower or
the editor support, except for the portions described in (d) and (e).

An "Independent Program" is a program, library or other work that is not Wiz
and is not based on Wiz, other than by using the Runtime Library through the
interfaces it provides: importing its modules, calling its definitions, being
compiled against it, or being linked with it.

A "Compiled Work" is anything produced by compiling an Independent Program
with a Wiz compiler, or by combining the result with the Runtime Library, in
any form: generated source code in another language (such as C or LLVM IR),
object code, a library, an executable, or code for another target (such as
WebAssembly or a hardware description).

1. Grant of additional permission.

You have permission to propagate and convey a Compiled Work under terms of
your choice, even though the Compiled Work contains portions of the Runtime
Library or is combined with it, and even though such a combination would
otherwise be covered by the GPL. You need not provide the source code of the
Independent Program, and the Independent Program and the Compiled Work need
not be licensed under the GPL.

2. What this Exception does not change.

  (a) The Runtime Library itself, and any modified version of it, remains
      under the GPL. If you convey the Runtime Library, or a modified version
      of it, other than as part of a Compiled Work, you must do so under the
      GPL (with or without this Exception, as you choose).

  (b) The rest of Wiz remains under the GPL without any additional
      permission. A work that is based on the compilers, checkers, kernels,
      grail, tower or the editor support is not an Independent Program.

  (c) This Exception gives no permission regarding software that is not part
      of Wiz. A Compiled Work may be linked with other libraries (for example
      GMP or a garbage collector); their own licences continue to apply.

  (d) This Exception does not invalidate any other reason why a Compiled Work
      might be covered by the GPL.

3. No warranty.

The disclaimer of warranty and the limitation of liability in sections 15 and
16 of GPLv3 apply to the Runtime Library and to this Exception.
